  "description": {
   "value": "<p>You are the crew's <strong>Medic</strong> - the one who keeps everyone else breathing. Your power is not Veil and not code; it is <strong>chemistry and skill</strong>. You run on <strong>Reagents</strong>: a strategic reserve of compounds, stims, patches, toxins, and antidotes you <strong>brew and pack on a respite</strong>. The bag you bring is the bag you have - unspent Reagents persist between encounters, but the kit only refills in downtime.</p><p>The Medic is <strong>fully mundane</strong>. You have no Veil access and no Resonance, so the Chrome chapter's magic-erosion rule is simply irrelevant to you - you are chrome-positive and augment freely. You are the <strong>flesh-side of the installer trio</strong> (Wrench = hardware, Technomancer = neural/soft-code, <strong>you</strong> = flesh), and the game's answer to Exposure clocks: rads, hypothermia, toxins, the slow-death conditions. Confiscate a Hacker's deck and silence a caster's Veil - you cannot take a doctor's training.</p><h3>Signatures &amp; Subclass</h3><p>Three signatures cost no Reagents: <strong>First Aid</strong> (spend a Recovery to heal / stabilize the dying), <strong>Administer Dose</strong> (a basic compound - edge, temp Stamina, ignore a condition), and <strong>Diagnose</strong> (an Insight read of wounds, tox, and chrome). At Tier 5 you choose a subclass - <strong>Street-Doc</strong>, <strong>Corp-Medtech</strong>, or <strong>Ripperdoc</strong>.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> you choose your subclass, gain all three signatures, and pick an opening heroic ability. Every Tier after, you gain a new heroic ability and your Reagent capacity rises. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong>, where the apex <strong>Miracle Worker</strong> becomes reachable.</p>",
   "director": ""
  },
